    "Here's what the preview says will happen if you confirm. I haven't changed anything yet.\n\n**Actions:**\n1. **Remove the locally stored Google tokens.** This is the saved sign-in on this computer. Google's authorization for the app stays in place, because I won't revoke it remotely. Still, the app will no longer be connected to your Google account on this machine, so you'd need to reconnect later to pull fresh data from Google.\n2. **Cancel any active Google jobs** that are running.\n3. **Permanently delete the local Google records and retained raw responses.** This is the imported Google health data stored on this computer.\n\n**What stays:**\n- **Your Google Takeout copy** is not touched, because I've set the option to keep Takeout data.\n- **Google's authorization** is not revoked.\n- **Fitbit data** is not affected.\n\nThe deletion can't be undone from this tool. If you want a local copy of the Google data first, I can export it before deleting.\n\nDo you want me to go ahead? Reply **yes** to confirm, or tell me if you'd like the export first.",
